{"duration_api_ms":221086,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d2969334-9ac1-4981-b135-51aadb6d7df5","total_cost_usd":1.6353307999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":58,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103908,"cache_read_input_tokens":1939774,"output_tokens":20794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6543},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103908,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1237,"cache_read_input_tokens":104057,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":58,"outputTokens":20794,"cacheReadInputTokens":1939774,"cacheCreationInputTokens":103908,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.6353307999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6543,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ptk5BS6CereJUswCEUQ4GD","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout; for f in adapter/outgoing/payment/*.java application/shared/Payment*.java application/checkoutcompletion/submitpayment/*.java adapter/incoming/web/checkoutcompletion/PaymentPage*.java; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat -n $f; done; ls adapter/outgoing/payment","description":"Read payment port, adapters, use case, controller"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AmKAi9gihV1dDnBCtbVc5H","tool_input":{"command":"grep -n -B4 -A2 \"^\\s*[0-9]\\+\\.[0-9]\\+,\\?$\" src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/adapter/incoming/bootstrap/SampleDataInitializer.java | grep -v \"^\\-\\-$\" | head -60","description":"List seeded product prices"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TPSnXdKQdvbYpgier9rBQU","tool_input":{"command":"cat .claude/skills/factory-run/templates/decision.md.tmpl; ls .agents/factory/","description":"Read decision record template"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The plan is written, but it ends in a `## needs-human`: the story can't go on to the test stage until you answer one question.\n\n**What you need to decide:** the story's main scenario needs a browser test (`test-e2e`, Playwright) that checks two things. The review step shows, and the provider got exactly one payment request for 20.00 EUR. Against the shop that suite runs on today, neither can be set up:\n- **No provider stub.** The suite runs against a shop started beforehand (`bootRun` or the compose `shop` service) with no provider address, so the shop pays through the built-in stand-in. The test can't control the provider's answer or count its requests. Worse, it would pass today, so it would never fail first as the test stage requires.\n- **20.00 EUR can't be reached.** Every seeded price and shipping cost ends in .99 or .00, and no combination adds up to exactly 20.00. Adding a product through `POST /api/products` needs the `STAFF` role, which the suite doesn't have.\n\nThe question is in `.agents/factory/decisions/pay-through-the-provider-01.md`, with three options:\n- **A (my recommendation):** the browser suite starts its own provider stub on a fixed port, and the shop under it is started with the provider address pointing at it. That means changing the profile's `run:` line, `compose.yaml` and the `test-e2e` instructions in the README. The browser test checks the amount the review page shows, and an integration test under the same key checks the literal 20.00 EUR.\n- **B:** as A, plus a seeded product priced so 20.00 EUR is reachable. That puts a test-only item in the catalogue, which `project/product.md` warns against.\n- **C:** test the main scenario at the HTTP level in `src/test-integration` for this story instead of in a browser.\n\n**What the plan covers otherwise** (`tasks/pay-through-the-provider/plan.md`):\n- **Where it lives:** everything is in `checkout`. The designed and the generated context maps agree that the provider is reached over REST behind the existing `PaymentProvider` port, so no new context or relationship is needed.\n- **Changes:**\n  - A new REST adapter for the provider. It replaces the stand-in when an address is configured; without one the stand-in stays.\n  - The payment result can now say \"refused\" or \"unavailable\".\n  - The submit-payment use case raises the \"unavailable\" failure when the provider times out or can't be reached.\n  - The payment page controller shows the two exact messages from the story.\n  - New config: a provider address key in `application.yml`, empty by default.\n- **Test levels:** the refused and the slow-provider scenarios are integration tests that post the payment form, with the provider stubbed in WireMock. The main scenario waits on the decision.\n- **Existing tests:** none need to change. They all pay through the stand-in with no address configured, and none check the failure messages.\n- **Also in the plan:**\n  - Three glossary proposals: payment authorization, payment refusal, payment request.\n  - Assumptions I made, listed so they can be checked: the REST adapter replaces the stand-in rather than sitting beside it, how cancel and confirm are answered, and that any answer other than `201` or `402` counts as unavailable.\n  - A note that the provider description in `checkout/package-info.java` and `project/domain.md` will be out of date afterwards, left for the document stage.\n\nI ran no build, no tests and no other stage, including the story gate. I didn't consult the `dca-knowledge` catalog either, because the project's own declarations already settled how the provider is reached.","ttft_ms":2959,"type":"result","duration_ms":222779,"uuid":"b3615959-0d81-4373-aa51-10a2bffff79d","ttft_stream_ms":1731,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1731,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
